@bank all
// Head writer 4, for the career system (design-doc "Leave, missed shifts and being let go", 2026-10-17).
// The Career engineer sets the story flags: career.missed (a shift missed lately), career.low (the Chief's talk),
// career.verylow (the Captain's reprimand), career.bottom (the count to being let go is running), career.eve (let go
// tomorrow), career.lastday (the day you leave), career.up (climbing back after a step down), leave.booked (leave
// tomorrow), onleave (on leave today), leave.back (first workday after leave). Rename here if theirs differ.
// Tips and the closing card are said by nobody: the game shows the text. Keep tips free of exact numbers (the
// lead's defaults may change): "a few days", "every few weeks".

== career.tip.late
- Late for your shift. A little late is only a small dip. Be in the Works bay by eight.
- Shift starts at eight. Turning up late often adds up, so set off a bit earlier.

== career.tip.missed
- You missed a shift. That's a big hit to your work standing, with Works and the whole ship.
- Missed shifts add up. Turn up tomorrow and do good work, and your standing comes back.
- Need a day off? Book leave in Schedule on your device, and it won't count against you.

== career.tip.low
- Your work standing is low. Chief Calder wants to see you. It's on your Schedule.
- To climb back: be on shift by eight, finish jobs, and turn them in at the board.
- Not well? The infirmary first. Time there never counts against you.

== career.tip.verylow
- Your standing is very low. The Captain has asked to see you. It isn't too late.
- Every full shift helps. Every job turned in at the board helps more.

== career.tip.bottom
- You're at the bottom. A few more days like this and the Wren will let you go.
- One good shift stops the count. Go to the Works bay tomorrow, by eight.

== career.tip.up
- Your work standing is climbing. Keep turning up. People have noticed.
- Back on solid ground. Keep going: shift by eight, jobs to the board.

== career.tip.leave
- Need a day? Book leave in Schedule on your device, by the evening before.
- You only get a few leave days, and one more every few weeks. Spend them well.
- Booked leave by mistake? Cancel it in Schedule and you get the day back.
- Time in the infirmary when you're ill never uses up your leave.

== career.closing.title
- The Wren sails on

== career.closing.body
- You left on the Tern. The Wren sails on, and the people you met still talk about you.
- Somewhere a scrubber hums and nobody thanks the air. Thank you for your time aboard.
- The bunk is made up for someone new. Your friends kept your place at the table a while.

== career.closing.button
- Begin again

// Crew who know you a little: the everyday worried lines. Friends and the story crew have their own.
== career.worried
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.missed
- {hi}. Didn't see you on shift today. All right?
- Missed shift, I heard. Happens once. Just don't make it a habit.
? tier>=colleague flag:career.missed
- If something's keeping you from shift, say. Someone here can help.   #warm
? tier>=colleague flag:career.low
- Heard the Chief wants a word. She's fair. Go and hear her out.
- Calder's not a shouter. She'll tell you what's wrong once, plainly. Listen.
? tier>=colleague flag:career.verylow
- Up to the ready room? {sigh}. The Captain's kind. Still, go to your shift.   #warm
? tier>=colleague flag:career.up
- Saw you on shift this morning. Good. Keep that up.
- Things looking up? You look more like yourself.

== career.eve
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.eve
- I heard you're leaving tomorrow. I'm sorry. Look after yourself.
- Tomorrow, is it? The Wren won't be the same. Safe trip.
? tier>=colleague flag:career.eve
- Leaving tomorrow. I'm sorry it went this way. You were good company.   #warm

== career.bye
? tier>=acquaintance flag:career.lastday
- {bye}, {nick}. Safe trip on the Tern.
- Off today, then. Good luck out there. I mean it.
? tier>=colleague flag:career.lastday
- Go well. Turn up wherever you land. The rest comes.   #warm

== career.seeoff
? tier>=friend flag:career.lastday
- Came to see you off. Couldn't not.   #warm
- Window seat. Promise me.   #warm
- Write when you land. Proper Mail.   #warm

// Booking leave and coming back from it (the leave.* flags above).
== career.leave
? tier>=acquaintance flag:leave.booked
- Day off tomorrow? Good for you. Sleep in.
- Leave tomorrow! Anything planned, or just nothing at all?
? tier>=acquaintance flag:onleave
- Aren't you on leave? Go and do something nice.
- On leave and you're still here? Fair. Where else would you go?   #funny

== career.back
? tier>=acquaintance flag:leave.back
- {hi}. Back from leave? You look rested.
- Welcome back. The board missed you. Well, someone had to say it.   #funny
